note top of LobbyController
  Start calls GameSetup.createGame, GameScreenFactory.create, and
  ViewRouter.show in that order. If setup rejects the input with
  IllegalArgumentException, show the error and keep the lobby open.
  Data entry refreshes the lobby form.
end note

note top of GameScreenFactory
  Creates the views and controllers that need a session.
  All match controllers share that session. The table controller
  closes its subscription before routing back to the lobby.
end note

note top of GameTableController
  Owns the displayed overlay, selected build,
  and confirmed viewer. Clears private content when
  a handoff starts and waits for the next Ready.
  Subscribes on open and unsubscribes on close.
  Coalesces model updates and UI-only changes
  into a queued JavaFX refresh.
end note

note bottom of GameSession
  Owns setup order, roll and turn sequencing, interruption and resumption,
  score aggregation, and victory. Helpers implement the individual rules.
  Controller-facing actions validate actor and phase where applicable,
  call the helper, finish any match transition, and notify once.
  Rejected actions leave the match unchanged and report a domain error.
  Build, trade, and inventory queries forward or combine helper data.
  On a seven, queues required discards and saves ACTION as the resume phase.
  Calls initiateRobbery after the last discard, or immediately if none are due.
  A Knight saves the current phase and calls initiateRobbery immediately.
  Submitting a victim calls setRobberyTarget then conductRobbery.
  After a move or steal, an empty pending robbery means the turn can resume.
  The GUI reads the next discarder, legal destinations, or eligible victims
  through getRobberState and receives one session update per completed action.
  Development options combine purchase eligibility and pending card choices.
  Controllers request a hand only after the viewer confirms Ready.
  Final scores include hidden victory points once the match ends.
end note

note bottom of RobberyHelper
  Keeps PR #127's initiate, target selection, and transfer methods.
  The proposed move validates the actor and hex, moves the board piece,
  and finds eligible opponents. Clear the pending robbery after the steal
  or after a move with no eligible victim.
  A random steal needs read access to the victim's resource counts.
end note

note bottom of DiscardHelper
  Keeps PR #127's staged selection methods. The whole-selection overload
  lets GameSession submit a completed form in one call. Validate the
  required quantity and ownership before transferring cards to the bank.
end note

note bottom of GameBoard
  GameSetup starts the robber on the desert. Moving the piece updates
  its hex and which tile production skips. GameSession starts the workflow.
end note

note bottom of DevelopmentHelper
  Assumed API. Tracks purchase turns and legal card plays.
  After a successful Knight play, the session starts the robber workflow.
  Holds pending Year of Plenty, Monopoly, and Road Building choices.
  Applies submitted choices and checks legal free-road edges.
  Completes Road Building when both roads are placed or none can be placed.
  Counts hidden Victory Point cards for the session's victory check.
end note

note bottom of PurchaseHelper
  PR #123's paid build takes the actual piece. GameSession resolves
  the build type to an available piece before calling it.
  Proposed change to PR #123: return the exact purchased card so
  GameSession can call DevelopmentHelper.recordPurchase(card).
end note

note bottom of PlayerTradeHelper
  Uses the trade branch's object-based API and offer identity.
  GameSession maps GUI IDs to distinct active offers.
  Accept records agreement. Finalize transfers the resources.
  End turn expires outstanding offers.
end note

note bottom of BankResourceDistributor
  PR #123's finalizeProduction returns void. The board queues claims,
  and the distributor settles them against bank stock. GameSession can
  compare resource counts before and after to summarize actual payouts.
end note

note bottom of GameTableView
  Layout, rendering, and hit-testing.
  Tells controller what the player selected.
end note
@enduml
